    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "# Wellbore Geology Dataset Readiness Report",
        "id": "block_01"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Executive Summary\n\n- **The dataset is sequence-first, not row-first.** Train contains 773 horizontal wells with 5.09M horizontal rows; public test contains 3 wells with 14,151 rows to predict. Model validation should be grouped by well_id, not random rows.\n- **The target is TVT continuation.** `TVT_input` is known at the start of each horizontal well and missing over the prediction interval. In public test, every submission row maps exactly to a missing `TVT_input` row.\n- **Train has extra geology surfaces that public test does not expose.** Columns such as `ANCC`, `ASTNU`, `ASTNL`, `EGFDU`, `EGFDL`, and `BUDA` are useful for understanding the data but should not be used as ordinary model features for hidden test.\n- **GR coverage is incomplete.** `GR` is an important signal, but it has substantial missingness, so a baseline needs imputation or features robust to missing gamma-ray logs.",
        "id": "block_02"
      },
      {
        "type": "metric-strip",
        "cardIds": [
          "card_train_wells",
          "card_test_wells",
          "card_prediction_rows",
          "card_train_missing"
        ],
        "id": "block_03"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## File Layout and Modeling Grain\n\nThe raw Kaggle files now live under `datasets/`. Each well has one horizontal-well CSV and one typewell CSV; train also includes a PNG diagnostic plot per well. The natural modeling unit is a well sequence ordered by `MD`, while the submission unit is an individual missing `TVT_input` row.",
        "id": "block_04"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "table_schema",
        "id": "block_05"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Prediction Zones Are Long Tails\n\nThe hidden part of each well is usually most of the horizontal trajectory. This makes naive row-wise validation risky: adjacent rows leak trajectory behavior. Use GroupKFold or holdout wells for local validation.",
        "id": "block_06"
      },
      {
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "chart_prediction_share",
        "id": "block_07"
      },
      {
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "chart_test_zones",
        "id": "block_08"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "table_test_zones",
        "id": "block_09"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Missingness Drives Baseline Design\n\n`TVT_input` missingness defines the prediction interval. `GR` missingness is separate and material, so the first baseline should work even when gamma ray is absent. Train-only geology surface columns should be treated as diagnostic context, not production features.",
        "id": "block_10"
      },
      {
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "chart_missing",
        "id": "block_11"
      },
      {
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "chart_rows_hist",
        "id": "block_12"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "table_profile",
        "id": "block_13"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Typewell Context\n\nTypewell files provide a vertical reference curve with `TVT` and `GR`. In train they also include `Geology`, but test typewells omit geology labels. This supports feature ideas based on aligning horizontal `GR` to typewell `GR`, while keeping label-derived features out of the first hidden-test baseline.",
        "id": "block_14"
      },
      {
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "chart_geology",
        "id": "block_15"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. Build a no-ML baseline that extends the last known `TVT_input` by local slope.\n2. Build a tabular baseline using only test-available fields: `MD`, `X`, `Y`, `Z`, `GR`, and features derived from known `TVT_input`.\n3. Validate by held-out wells. Random row splits will overstate quality.\n4. Add typewell alignment features after the baseline is stable.\n\n## Caveats and Assumptions\n\nThis artifact summarizes local CSV files after moving the dataset into `datasets/`. It uses aggregate and sampled tables to stay within the interactive artifact size limit; raw row-level data remains available in the dataset folder.",
        "id": "block_16"
      }
    ]
  },
